rem Open Chess Positions
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=628

use numbers
use io
use cli

arg N integer = 100000000

rem Rows read top down, a position is
rem closed when a run of pawns on
rem consecutive rows holds consecutive
rem rising columns, and either starts
rem on the top row (a block B(j) with
rem columns n - j to n - 1 first) or in
rem column 0, and ends on the bottom
rem row or in the last column. B(j)
rem and C(m) are exclusive among
rem themselves, B(n) = C(n - 1) is the
rem identity and B(j) C(m) leaves
rem (n - j - m - 1)! free, so
rem f = n! - 2 sum k! + 1 + sum s
rem (n - 1 - s)!, k = 0 to n - 1 and
rem s = 1 to n - 1, with a running k!.
M = 1008691207
rem Fs = k! for k = 0 to n, Ps its
rem prefix sums; sum s (n - 1 - s)! is
rem the sum of Ps up to n - 2.
Fs = 1 to N scan * with 1 mod M
Ps = Fs scan + mod M
Fk = Fs (N)
S1 = Ps (N - 1)
T = (Ps (0 to N - 2)) sum
Answer = (Fk - 2 * S1 + T + 1) mod M
Answer print
